 "observations": [
  "The page number «248» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it. The page has no signature. The heading of part IV (L01) is centred in the sans-serif type of regular weight of the headings of parts I-III (pp. [241] and 247, JP2 0275 and 0281); L02 below it in italics, its parentheses and point upright. Below the list a short centred double rule ends the glossary; the rest of the page is blank. Through the paper the print of p. 249 (JP2 0283) shows faintly, reversed; not transcribed.",
  "L03-L14: numbered lines of five parts, written as rows of a table: the name of Tab. 3a, «=» with the Syriac name in Latin letters (L03-L06 with the numbers «(I.)» and «(II.)» of the two Teshrīn and the two Kānūn), «=» with the Latin name of the month, and «(des julian. Jahres).» (L03) or the ditto marks «( — — ).» (L04-L14); the «=» signs of each part stand one below the other. «qᵉdīm», «ḥᵉrai», «Shᵉbāṭ» and «Ḥᵉzīrān» with the e raised, written {sup:e}; in L11 the dot under the Ḥ is set low, near the T of «Tāmūz» in the next line, which has no dot.",
  "Checked against the text: the names of the first part are those of the head of Tab. 3a (p. 114, JP2 0146), in the same order, with «Hezi-ren» divided there; the Latin names of the months as in the same head (Octobr. to Septbr.), the Syrian year of the tables beginning with Teshrīn I = October (p. 40, JP2 0072)."
 ],
